BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introductory Piano: Adult Learning Circles in 4 Sessions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T160000
UID:69e77fe6bd9a3c316a544e42@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to learn to play the piano? Join us for 
 four small adult (18+ with no age limit) learning circles consisting of f
 our participants led by a professional pianist. You will learn the basic p
 iano including note recognition\, finger placing\, and simple songs. There
  will be opportunities for one-on-one instruction for each participant at 
 a baby grand piano.\nFor absolute beginners only. One time registration fo
 r all four sessions starts on Monday\, May 25\, 2026 at 10am online.  Pl
 ease do not register if you have previously participated at the piano circ
 les at the Toronto Public Library.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e77fe6bd9a3c316a544e42
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sinye Tang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T235959
UID:6a299f022ea730c17ab5e09b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Sinye Tang are 
 on display at Don Mills Branch.\nSinye Tang (she/her) is a Chinese-Canadia
 n artist\, food enthusiast\, and amateur kayaker residing in Toronto. Her 
 artwork is informed by urban forays into nature and in search of deliciou
 s bites. She enjoys starting her watercolours in nature or on the water\, 
 and collaborates often with her husband\, Evan Manuella\, on line and was
 h.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Pu
 blic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at loc
 ations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural
  interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed 
 during branch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a299f022ea730c17ab5e09b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sharon Alex
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T235959
UID:6a20399b748daf857d5ab337@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Sharon Alex
  are on display at Albion Branch\nSharon is an artist based in Toronto. S
 he paints in watercolours and loves photography. Her poetry explores her i
 nner most thoughts and hope she opens something within yourself as well\n
 "I'm inspired by animals and nature and poetry. My purpose is to tap into 
 the intimate and make you pause and explore what is important to you".\nTh
 is exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Li
 brary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations 
 across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural intere
 sts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during 
 Albion branch's open hours. Please check the\nAlbion branch\npage before y
 ou visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto credit: Sharon Alex\,\nThe Monar
 ch\, Photograph\, 8x10.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a20399b748daf857d5ab337
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Maggie Broda
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T235959
UID:6a3d4ce368c8e9ce674db9ec@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Maggie Broda ar
 e on display at North York Central Library in an exhibit.\nOntario Based 
 Freelance Visual Artist\, Maggie Broda is a long time Muskoka Arts and Cra
 fts member\, BFA\, Associate of OCA\, Visual Artist\, Writer\, and Educat
 or. Her work is in private collections throughout Canada\, she is the OCAD
  University Alumni Association’s President. Maggie is a contemporary pa
 inter\, interviewer/writer and art advocate. President Emeritus of the Wom
 en’s Art Association of Canada\, Muskoka Arts and Craft Member\, Executi
 ve Board Member at John B Aird."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhi
 bits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artis
 ts to exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim 
 to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoo
 ds.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nNorth York Central Library\nopen 
 hours.\nFree. All are welcome.\nArtist:  Maggie Broda\nPiece:  Travell
 ing with Hope\nMedium:  Acrylic on Canvas
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Floor 2 of North York Central Librar
 y
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d4ce368c8e9ce674db9ec
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Money Management and Access to Government Benefits
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T120000
UID:69e1271c129f12743838f4d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to take control of your finances and make your money
  work for you. This practical workshop facilitated by a financial empowerm
 ent staff member from North York Community House will help you understand 
 your income and expenses\, create a realistic budget\, start saving\, and 
 learn how to access government benefits you may be eligible for\, helping 
 you build a stronger and more secure financial foundation.\nDrop-in welcom
 e!\nNo registration required.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e1271c129f12743838f4d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
