BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T200000
UID:69960daf4a9fd98b7f7ed8f3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on Mon
 day\, May 25 from 5-7 PM.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Monday\,\nonce a w
 eek for 8 weeks\, June 1 - July 20\, 2026\, 5-8pm\n. Registration closes 
 after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks
  and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will
  be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGer
 stein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely
  responsible for the protection of personal information collected through
  the program registration process.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69960daf4a9fd98b7f7ed8f3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Managing Invasive Plants Around Your Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T200000
UID:69c7fcfe1e64afd01e6543e4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for a presentation o
 n invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. Learn how to ide
 ntify these species\, understand their impact\, and how to manage them.\nY
 ou’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing n
 ative habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeowners\, and anyone interested
  in urban ecology.\nNo registration. Drop-in.\nThis program is part of TPL
 's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto P
 ublic Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Downstairs
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c7fcfe1e64afd01e6543e4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de Cedarbrae
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T200000
UID:6a108ed98360de907d880d72@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aimez-vous lire en français? Avez-vous envie de participer à
  des discussions autour des livres dans une ambiance conviviale et déten
 due?\nRejoignez notre club de lecture en français! Venez échanger vos po
 ints de vue\, analyser ce qui vous a marqué avec le regard d'autres lecte
 urs\, et faire de belles découvertes littéraires.\nOn se réunit le 29 j
 uin pour découvrir\n« Manikanetish » de Naomi Fontaine\n. Le livre sera
  disponible en prêt à la succursale de Cedarbrae\n\, au comptoir de prê
 t\, à partir du 29 mai 2026.\nSi vous voulez en savoir plus sur nos clubs
  de lectures\, veuillez nous envoyer un courriel à\nprogrammesenfrancais@
 tpl.ca\nVeuillez noter que ce programme s’adresse aux personnes francoph
 ones ainsi qu’à celles ayant un niveau avancé en français. Il est né
 cessaire de pouvoir lire\, discuter et critiquer un livre avec une aisance
  de communication en français.\nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre frança
 is mais que vous avez plutôt un niveau débutant ou intermédiaire\, nous
  vous encourageons à découvrir nos cercles de conversation.\nLe sous-tit
 rage en direct ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\,
  les services d’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont di
 sponibles sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux sema
 ines à l’avance à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Auditorium (FCCR)\, first floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a108ed98360de907d880d72
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Festival Select: The Passenger (Michelangelo Antonioni\, 1975)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T203000
UID:698fa3db94297d3600ac23fe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the Society and Recreation department of the North York C
 entral Library for monthly screenings of fiction and non-fiction films tha
 t push the boundaries of the medium. This month we are showing Michelangel
 o Antonioni's\nThe Passenger\n(1975).\nSynopsis (Criterion Pictures): A j
 ournalist researching a documentary in the Sahara Desert meets a gunrunner
  who dies suddenly. When the journalist notices that they have a similar a
 ppearance\, he assumes the recently deceased's identity and accepts the co
 nsequences that it brings.\nNo registration required.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698fa3db94297d3600ac23fe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
