BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Lama Al Ghatrif
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T235959
UID:6a0506a0caf93436005bc949@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Lama Al Ghatrif
  are on display at Agincourt Branch.\nRaised between Syria and the UAE\, L
 ama is an internationally trained architect who moved to Canada in 2019. H
 er creative journey is rooted in a lifelong passion for drawing that preda
 tes her architectural career. Since graduating in 2010\, Lama has balance
 d the technical discipline of design with a dedicated fine arts practice\,
  specializing in realistic charcoal portraiture and expressive mixed-media
 . Her work explores the intersection of structural precision and emotive s
 torytelling—a global perspective shaped by a life of transition across b
 orders and disciplines.\n"\nArchitecture provides the framework for our li
 ves\, but drawing captures the essence of our living."\nThis exhibit is pa
 rt of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides 
 space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city
 . These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city
  and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nAgincourt\nbra
 nch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Lama Al Ghatrif\; c
 harcoal and golden leaf on paper\; "Finding the Light"
LOCATION:Agincourt\, First floor hallway towards the Children's Department
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0506a0caf93436005bc949
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
