UID:6a147b92748daf857d59b703@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout June\, works by artist Saranga Kotambar are on disp
 lay at Mimico Centennial branch.\nSaranga is a self-taught artist speciali
 zing in watercolours and acrylics. Her work is driven by passion and guide
 d by instinct rather than formal training. Through each piece\, she captur
 es emotion\, depth\, and her unique vision of the world\, with paintings t
 hat reflect the bright side of life.\n"My work is inspired by elements of 
 Indian culture and the emotional connections I've shared with people aroun
 d me while growing up. I explore memories\, traditions\, and everyday mome
 nts through colour\, form\, and storytelling. Each piece reflects a person
 al journey and deep sense of belonging.".\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\n
 Art Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for loc
 al artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhib
 its aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neig
 hbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nMimico Centennial\nbranch o
 pen hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Mezzanine
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a147b92748daf857d59b703
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
