 r work is in private collections throughout Canada\, she is the OCAD Unive
 rsity Alumni Association’s President. Maggie is a contemporary painter\,
  interviewer/writer and art advocate. President Emeritus of the Women’s 
 Art Association of Canada\, Muskoka Arts and Craft Member\, Executive Boar
 d Member at John B Aird.\n"My paintings express a passion for creativity a
 nd the environment both urban and natural\, created in acrylic with brush 
 and palette knife. The texture and movement captures the poetic spirituali
 ty that is inherent in art."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits 
 Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to
  exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to re
 flect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\n
 The exhibit can be viewed during North York Central Library open hours.\nF
 ree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Maggie Broda\; End of the Tra
 il.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd floor Gallery Space
