BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kick Off Your Health This Soccer Season! ⚽
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T120000
UID:6a286db3c7d3cd58005f3114@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore healthy habits\, preventative care\, and the important
  role family doctors play in supporting your health.\nJoin us for an engag
 ing health promotion webinar focused on staying healthy while enjoying the
  excitement of FIFA. Whether you’re cheering on your favourite team\, ho
 sting watch parties\, or staying up for late-night matches\, it’s import
 ant to prioritize your health and well-being along the way.\nThis session 
 will explore:\nTips for managing chronic conditions during busy events and
  irregular routines\nHealthy habits you can incorporate while enjoying gam
 e days\nThe importance of preventative care and staying connected to healt
 hcare supports\nWhy having a family doctor matters and how they can suppor
 t your long-term health\nOur speakers will also share local resources and 
 practical strategies to help you stay connected to care while balancing ev
 eryday life and the excitement of the tournament.\nCome learn\, ask questi
 ons\, and celebrate the connection between community\, wellness\, and the 
 world’s game.\nThis program is presented by Toronto Public Library in co
 llaboration with the\nWest Toronto Ontario Health Team\n(OHT)\, a network 
 of over 40 local health and social service providers working together to i
 mprove the health and well-being of communities in West Toronto. This sess
 ion is being delivered by staff from\nLAMP Community Health Centre\n\, a m
 ember organization of the West Toronto Ontario Health Team.\nYour Health M
 atters\nThis program is part of Toronto Public Library’s\nYour Health Ma
 tters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted health programs and resources to 
 help people make informed decisions about their health. Learn more by expl
 oring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis
  virtual event is free to join but registration is required.\nPlease regis
 ter on Eventbrite\n.\nOnce registered\, you’ll receive an email with det
 ails on how to join the session.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a286db3c7d3cd58005f3114
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NFB Film Screening: Wilfred Buck
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T150000
UID:6a18447cf56bd86e00b2b71d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a\nNational Film Board of Canada\nfilm screening t
 his National Indigenous History Month\, and learn more about Cree Elder an
 d astronomer\,\nWilfred Buck\n!\nHis name is He Has Dreamt a Dream and Kee
 ps It\, but most know him as Wilfred Buck\, the Star Man. In his own words
 \, he is “of the fresh-out-of-the-bush\, partly civilized\, colonized\, 
 displaced people.” A charismatic Cree Elder with a sly wit\, Wilfred is 
 known for collecting the knowledge of Cree astronomy and sharing it across
  generations. His teachings have taken him from lecture halls to sweat lod
 ges\, transcending the boundaries of Western science. Intimate yet expansi
 ve\, Wilfred Buck is a time-travelling road trip through a harrowing histo
 ry of displacement and racism\, from growing up in 1960s Northern Manitoba
  to Wilfred’s reconnection with the cosmological wisdom of his people. C
 ombining cinematic re-enactments\, archival footage and beautiful celestia
 l imagery with Buck’s unmistakable laugh\, director Lisa Jackson takes u
 s on a journey to the space beyond\, and to the spaces between us all.\nDo
 cumentary is rated PG\, run-time approximately 96 minutes.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Auditorium (FCCR)\, first floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a18447cf56bd86e00b2b71d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
