BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Zoë Craig
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T235959
UID:6a1de40e4407827f8aa1e53d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Zoë Craig is a Toronto-based printmaker specializing in silks
 creen with a BFA from Queen’s University. She works out of Open Studio a
 nd teaches silkscreen at the TDSB. Her passion for printmaking began in ch
 ildhood\, taking classes at the Art Gallery of Ontario. Zoë is an award-w
 inning artist with work held in several prominent local collections\, incl
 uding Ernst & Young\, Toronto-Dominion Bank\, and the City of Toronto. Zo
 ë is represented by ArtMatch.ca.\nZoë’s creative process emphasizes la
 yered compositions using transparent\, richly coloured inks to build textu
 re\, depth\, and a painterly quality within her Silkscreen prints. Drawin
 g inspiration from urban and natural landscapes\, Zoë creates dynamic sil
 kscreen prints based on photographs she takes of neighbourhoods she’s l
 ived in\, visited\, or found visually compelling. Her goal is to breathe l
 ife into each scene through careful layering and gestural mark-making.\nT
 his exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toronto Public Library
  provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations acros
 s the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests o
 f the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nRich
 view\nbranch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Richview\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1de40e4407827f8aa1e53d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
