BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Georgia Wang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T235959
UID:6a1de0498ea300e2631a3582@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Georgia Wan
 g are on display at Leaside branch in an exhibit titled\nWorks by Georgia 
 Wang\n.\nGeorgia Wang is a classical pianist who studied at the Mason Gros
 s School of the Arts (BM 2019-2023) and the The Glenn Gould School (ADP 20
 23-2025)\, as well as a visual artist and poet. Recent projects include gi
 ving piano recitals in Xiamen and Shanghai in June 2025. Georgia has exhib
 ited with the Vancouver Visual Arts Foundation's Art Downtown in the summ
 er of 2023\, and organized an art showcase in July 2024 including a readin
 g of her poetry book\nGoing and Being\n(2021).\n"Making art is a practice 
 that helps me to reflect on and tune into my experience of being in the wo
 rld. I hope to inspire a sense of beauty and aliveness that makes one inno
 cent again to the wonders of life and nature. The process is empowering an
 d supportive to myself. I think that my role as an artist is to try to get
  to heart of something\, and to express myself as honestly as I can.”\nT
 his exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toronto Public Library
  provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations acros
 s the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests o
 f the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nLeas
 ide Branch\nopen hours. Please check the Leaside Branch page before your v
 isit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Georgia Wang\; Title 
 of Piece: Lake Loraine Mountains\, Banff\; Medium: Acrylic\; Size/Dimensio
 ns: up to 20 x 25 cm
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1de0498ea300e2631a3582
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Life on Toronto Waterfront - Works by Mariana 
 Hernandez
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T235959
UID:6a353ca8414ef43d009767d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of Mariana Hernandez
  are on display at Oakwood Village Library and Arts Centre.\nMariana Her
 nandez is a Toronto based\, native to Chile\, multi-media artist living in
  Toronto since 1977. She studied Fine Art at OCAD and has also expanded he
 r skills as a self-taught learner. Vibrant colors\, strong line work in dr
 awings and a love and admiration for bodies of water and urban settings ar
 e her trademarks. She is also currently an art educator teaching to Non-P
 rofits across Toronto & GTA. She lives & works in the new Bayside\ncommun
 ity at Waterfront Toronto East Bayfront area.\nToronto's waterfront neighb
 orhood is a vast network of harbor slips\, public art displays and a hot s
 pot for tourism. As Toronto's city population grows\, new waterfront neig
 hborhoods are built\, leisure activity on the water also grows\, and there
  is more awareness of the work that happens on the inner harbor such as b
 oats and ships that bring sugar\, and dredge the Keating channel. My sketc
 hes and drawings bring to life the everyday scenes I see\nthroughout the s
 easons here in East Bayfront.\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\
 nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhib
 it their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect 
 the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe ex
 hibit can be viewed during Oakwood Village Library and Arts Centre open ho
 urs.
LOCATION:Oakwood Village Library and Arts Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a353ca8414ef43d009767d4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Astigmatic Variations by Ross Stockwell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T235959
UID:69f3c3a91d82f930d3cb2ce1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Ross Stockw
 ell are on display at\nDeer Park branch\n.\nRoss Stockwell is based in Tor
 onto\, Ontario. Borne of a mindful presence\, he notices whimsy and intrig
 ue in unlikely places. His work is eclectic\, unified by illuminating odd
 ities and the play of geometric forms. He expresses subjective experience\
 , exploring states of being\, felt-sense moods\, and emotions in an inani
 mate context. Stockwell has shown his work at Spectra (May 2022\, Hutchiso
 n Road)\; G44’s Members Gallery (January 2023\; Dissolution) and Spectr
 a\, May 2024\; Astigmatic Variations)\n"Astigmatic Variations” is an ong
 oing project where Stockwell captures images using time exposures and in-c
 amera movement. Textured overlays are applied to render artistic interpre
 tations depicting mood states of longing\, melancholy\, and dissolution\, 
 often implicit in our experience of time and imperfection. Stockwell has 
 an appreciation for the immediate perception of things while being aware o
 f their implied history and their dynamic trajectory toward some future."
 \nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Publi
 c Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locati
 ons across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural in
 terests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed dur
 ing Deer Park's open hours. Please check the\nDeer Park branch\npage befo
 re your visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nSolitary Figure\nImage credit: Art
 ist: Ross Stockwell\nTitle of Piece: Solitary Figure\nMedium: Photo-Inkje
 t Print - Framed\nSize/Dimensions: Medium
LOCATION:Deer Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f3c3a91d82f930d3cb2ce1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
