BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Your Niche: Building A Business Around What Makes You Diff
 erent
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T200000
UID:6a2c8a981e67cd9cb3398f8a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:One of the biggest challenges entrepreneurs face is trying to 
 appeal to everyone. In reality\, the strongest businesses are often built 
 around a clearly defined audience and a unique point of difference.\nIn th
 is interactive workshop\, participants will explore how to identify their 
 target audience\, clarify their value proposition\, and position themselve
 s more effectively in the marketplace. Whether you're launching a new vent
 ure or refining an existing business\, you'll leave with practical tools t
 o help define what makes your business stand out.\nAll\n sessions are inte
 ractive and participants are encouraged to bring \nquestions related to th
 eir own business or entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Melanie C
 ruickshank is a founder and brand-side operator with over 15 years of expe
 rience building\, launching\, and scaling beauty and personal care brands.
  As the founder of da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from product dev
 elopment and retail strategy to e-commerce growth and national partnership
 s. Known for her hands-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a founde
 r’s accountability and a deep understanding of what it takes to build br
 ands that perform in market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2c8a981e67cd9cb3398f8a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
