DESCRIPTION:In this\n8-week course\n\, learn how to build a strong web pre
 sence for your business in Toronto\, whether you’re launching something 
 new or already running one. Explore how to create a website using WordPres
 s and understand why it remains a powerful tool\, even in the age of AI we
 bsite builders. While AI can help you get started quickly\, WordPress giv
 es you full control over your content\, updates\, and long-term growth. By
  the end\, you’ll feel more confident managing your own website\, saving
  costs while strengthening your marketing at the same time.\nParticipants 
 should plan to attend all 8 of the following d\nates:\nMay 6\, May 13\,\n
 May 20\nJune 3\, June 17\, June 24\nJuly 8\, July 15\nRegistration is requ
 ired for the full series\n. This program is hosted by the Business\, Scien
 ce and Technology department. Please visit the 4th floor service desk or c
 all (416) 395-5613 for more information.\nThis program is part of the\n"Bu
 ilding your own Website for Small Business" Program Series (Newcomer strea
 m)\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
