UID:6a369ba843b41b3d006fc4ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a beginner or an experienced artist\, our Artis
 t Circle program offers a welcoming space to reduce stress\, explore new a
 rt techniques\, and connect with fellow art appreciators.\nJoin the Langua
 ge\, Literature\, and Fine Arts Department for a workshop on how to write 
 three common forms of poetry: acrostic\, blackout\, and cinquain. This beg
 inner-friendly workshop will begin with a short lesson introducing each po
 etic form\, with examples to help spark ideas and show how flexible and pl
 ayful poetry can be.\nMost of the workshop will be dedicated to hands-on w
 riting time\, giving participants the chance to experiment with different 
 formats\, play with language\, and create their own original poems in a re
 laxed and supportive environment. At the end of the session\, participants
  will be invited to share one of their poems with the group\, though shari
 ng is completely optional. Participants will also receive a recommended r
 eading list to continue exploring poetry after the program.\nAll supplies 
 will be provided. Just bring your curiosity\, creativity\, and a willing
 ness to try something new!
