BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Concerts - China Court Duo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T200000
UID:6a1a008bc6a1dc3d00d70f28@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:China Court Duo features three elegant Chinese traditional ins
 truments Pipa (Chinese lute) \, Xun (Globular vessel flute)\, and Dizi (Ba
 mboo flute). The two masterful musicians Wen Zhao (PIpa) and Yucheng Zhang
  (Xun and Dizi) focuses on performing Court repertoires and traditional fo
 lk music from the Ming and Qing dynasty\, the program includes spirited an
 cient poem repertories in China\, and Wen Zhao's recent composition for th
 e silk string Pipa Dynasty\, a suite work traces the history of the Pipa t
 hrough three of China's imperial dynasties.\nFor more information\, contac
 t the Arts Department at 416-393-7157.\nThursday\, July 23\, 2025\, 7\n:00
  – 8:00 p.m.\nBeeton Hall\, Toronto Reference Library
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1a008bc6a1dc3d00d70f28
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T203000
UID:6a10b7db43b41b3d006870c6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated learning circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting Essenti
 als course. By completing this program\, you will earn a Google Prompting 
 Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn and social media
  profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for those with som
 e experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articles\, assignmen
 ts and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Skills\n: How to
  use a prompting framework to create a desired output with GenAI\; how to 
 evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStrategies to dra
 ft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, and more.\nDat
 a & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and use GenAI respon
 sibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to use prompt cha
 ining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and reuse your best 
 prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary s
 taff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting Essentials speci
 alization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work to
 gether through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to a
 ttending all four learning circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI Re
 commended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the AI
  Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\nReg
 ister once on the first session of this event series\, in order to attend 
 all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid email address\n.\nA valid TPL 
 library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions (
 online via Zoom\, date: July 9\, 16\, 23\,30 )\nRegistration is a two-ste
 p procedure. First\, participants must complete their registration through
  this page. After this step\, library staff will follow up to request addi
 tional information in order to complete the registration.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10b7db43b41b3d006870c6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
