BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monday Afternoon at the Movies!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T160000
UID:6a39a6d090cc4e3a790ff8c6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come enjoy an afternoon at the Port Union Cinema!\nOver the co
 urse of the summer we will be showing a series of Studio Ghibli films.\nTh
 e schedule will be as follows:\nMonday July 13: My Neighbour Totoro\nFollo
 w the adventures of Satsuki and her four year old sister Mei as they disco
 ver their new neighbor is a mysterious forest spirit named Totoro who can 
 only be seen by the eyes of a child. As Totoro introduces the girls to his
  extraordinary friends\, they embark on the journey of a lifetime.\nMonday
  July 27: Ponyo\nA young boy named Sosuke rescues a goldfish named Ponyo\,
  and they embark on a fantastic journey of friendship and discovery before
  Ponyo's father\, a powerful sorcerer\, forces her to return to her home i
 n the sea. Ponyo's desire to be human upsets the delicate balance of natur
 e and triggers a gigantic storm. Only Ponyo's mother\, a beautiful sea god
 dess\, can restore nature's balance and make Ponyo's dreams come true.\nMo
 nday August 10: Spirited Away\nA young girl\, Chihiro\, finds herself trap
 ped in a strange new world of spirits and beasts. When her parents undergo
  a mysterious transformation\, she must call on the courage she never knew
  she had to free herself and return her family to the outside world.\nMond
 ay August 24: Kiki's Delivery Service\nA young witch named Kiki and her ch
 atty black cat Jiji befriend a bakery owner. Kiki is an enterprising young
  girl\, but she must follow tradition in order to become a full-fledged wi
 tch. Landing in a far-off city\, and with the help of her new friend\, she
  sets up a high-flying delivery service and begins a wonderful experience 
 of independence and responsibility as she finds her place in the world.\nT
 his is a\ndrop in\nprogram.\nNo registration required.\nThis is a BYoP eve
 nt. (Bring Your Own Popcorn.)**
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a39a6d090cc4e3a790ff8c6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
