BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Modern Marketing: Building Awareness Without a Big Budget
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T200000
UID:6a2c8a9b1e67cd9cb3398f8c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Many entrepreneurs assume they need a large marketing budget t
 o grow their business. The reality is that some of the most effective mark
 eting strategies cost very little and rely more on consistency\, creativit
 y\, and connection.\nJoin us for a discussion on modern marketing approach
 es including content creation\, community building\, partnerships\, referr
 als\, and creator-led marketing. Participants will explore practical ways 
 to increase visibility\, attract customers\, and build momentum without re
 lying heavily on paid advertising.\nAll sessions are interactive and parti
 cipants are encouraged to bring questions related to their own business or
  entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Melanie Cruickshank is a fou
 nder and brand-side operator with over 15 years of experience building\, l
 aunching\, and scaling beauty and personal care brands. As the founder of 
 da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from product development and retail
  strategy to e-commerce growth and national partnerships. Known for her ha
 nds-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a founder’s accountabilit
 y and a deep understanding of what it takes to build brands that perform i
 n market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2c8a9b1e67cd9cb3398f8c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
