DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T160000
UID:6a355a7acaf934360064362a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\, August 5\, 12\, 19 and 26 from 9:30-12.\nRegistration is
  a two-step process. First\, participants must complete their registration
  through this page. After this step\, library staff will follow up to requ
 est additional information in order to complete the registration.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a355a7acaf934360064362a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Colson Whitehead: Cool Machine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T200000
UID:6a26dfeb8d1b82ca9f7869e8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Two-time Pulitzer Prize-winner Colson Whitehead discusses the 
 magnificent final volume of his Harlem Trilogy.\nCool Machine returns us t
 o the world of successful business owner/master fence Ray Carney as he gam
 bles on one last heist to support his beloved wife\, but finds himself ent
 angled with a legendary criminal mastermind.\nStill haunted by his inabili
 ty to save his cousin Freddie years earlier\, Carney comes out of retireme
 nt to team up with friend and partner in crime\, Pepper\, for a chance to 
 rescue Freddie’s son from the violent forces of the city\, even if it me
 ans risking the safety and security he’s spent decades building for his 
 family.\nWith his trademark pitch-perfect prose\, Whitehead magnificently 
 brings to life 1980s New York\, painting a portrait of a city and a family
  in transition.\nColson Whitehead speaks with Elamin Abdelmahmoud about C
 ool Machine and the journey of bringing his acclaimed\, bestselling trilog
 y to its triumphant conclusion.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books ava
 ilable for purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nColson Whitehead\nElam
 in Abdelmahmoud\nRead more:\nCool Machine : A Novel\nCrook Manifesto\nHarl
 em Shuffle\nSon of Elsewhere\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and B
 luma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floo
 r\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registr
 ation required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that t
 he greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaran
 teed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first
  served.\nBar:\nBeer/wine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\n***
 \nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host loca
 l and international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about t
 heir new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey 
 following the program. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, 2nd Floo
 r
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a26dfeb8d1b82ca9f7869e8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Own Website for Small Business (Focus: Women Entrepr
 eneurs)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T200000
UID:6a2720c943b41b3d006cd09c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Having a personal website is essential for any small business.
  This\n8-week course\nwill cover everything from the basic fundamentals an
 d tools of WordPress all the way to the platform's advanced features that 
 support promoting and running a small business. Participants are encourage
 d to bring their own laptop\, but it is not required to attend.\nRegistrat
 ion is required for the full series. Participants are expected to attend a
 ll sessions on the following dates:\nJuly 22\nJuly 29\nAugust 5\nAugust 12
 \nAugust 19\nAugust 26\nSeptember 2\nSeptember 9\nThis program is hosted b
 y the Business\, Science and Technology department. Please visit the 3rd f
 loor service desk or call (416) 393-7149 for more information.\nThis progr
 am is part of the\n"Building your own Website for Small Business" Program 
 Series (Women Entrepreneurs stream)\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 2\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2720c943b41b3d006cd09c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mentorship & Community: Why Relationships Matter In Business
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T200000
UID:6a2d5e8b8d1b82ca9f79aec3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:No entrepreneur builds a business alone. Mentors\, peers\, col
 laborators\, and professional networks can all play an important role in h
 elping entrepreneurs navigate challenges and uncover new opportunities.\nT
 his\n session explores the value of mentorship and community in \nentrepre
 neurship. Participants will learn where to find mentors\, how to \nbuild m
 eaningful professional relationships\, and how to create a support\n netwo
 rk that can contribute to long-term growth and success.\nAll\n sessions ar
 e interactive and participants are encouraged to bring \nquestions related
  to their own business or entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Mel
 anie Cruickshank is a founder and brand-side operator with over 15 years o
 f experience building\, launching\, and scaling beauty and personal care b
 rands. As the founder of da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from produ
 ct development and retail strategy to e-commerce growth and national partn
 erships. Known for her hands-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a 
 founder’s accountability and a deep understanding of what it takes to bu
 ild brands that perform in market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2d5e8b8d1b82ca9f79aec3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
