BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: Rochdale: Dream Tower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T151500
UID:69ea39fb213814b1b524d47c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Dream Tower\n(1994\, Dir. Ron Mann) tells the tale of Rochdale
  College from its idealistic conception to drug addled demise.  Rochdale
  College (1968-1975) was an anti-institution where idealism and hedonism c
 onverged. Born out of the 1960’s activism against the repressive tendenc
 ies of traditional top-down university administration\, it sought a more a
 uthentic\, anti-hierarchal mode of learning combined with cooperative livi
 ng. It attracted students eager to learn and hippies experimenting with co
 untercultural ways of being. The mix was eventually subsumed by a bikers i
 nto North America's largest open drug market before it was closed for good
 .
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ea39fb213814b1b524d47c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: Dream Tower\, Rochdale College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T153000
UID:6a1b2e2ec6a1dc3d00d73ad3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:From 1968-1975\, Rochdale College offered a revolutionary educ
 ation in a cooperative living and learning environment. The original co-op
  housing venture integrated a school to avoid paying property taxes\, but 
 by the end few were paying their rent and the experiment collapsed from th
 e financial strain. In between\, there were many positive developments inc
 luding healthcare\, publishing\, theatre and daycare initiatives\, but cri
 minal infiltration doomed the project.\nDream Tower\n(dir. Ron Mann 1994) 
 documents the heady time of hippies and intellectual liberation mixing adv
 enturous students with motorcycle gangs and drug dealers at Rochdale Colle
 ge.\nThe program will begin with a short PowerPoint Toronto Star photos of
  Rochdale and there will be an optional discussion after the film.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1b2e2ec6a1dc3d00d73ad3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
