SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T130000
UID:6a14631e0c0f2c4503fb337b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participants
  will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-week 
 WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections\,
  relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, and
  more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.\n
 Interested in learning more? Drop in for the\ninformation session\non Thur
 sday\, September 3\, 2026 from 10:00am-12:00pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nev
 ery Thursday\, once a week for 8 weeks\, September 10 - October 29\, 2026\
 , 10:00am-1:00pm\n. Registration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC 
 Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for
  all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThi
 s program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiati
 ve\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible for the protection of p
 ersonal information collected through the program registration process.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Basement Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a14631e0c0f2c4503fb337b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
