 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Monday\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, August 
 10 - October 5\, 2026\, 5-8 pm\n.\n*Note: Library closed for statutory hol
 iday on September 7\nRegistration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC
  Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided fo
 r all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nT
 his program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initia
 tive\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible for the protection of
  \npersonal information collected through the program registration \nproce
 ss.
